    "title": "Property Tax Elimination",
    "url": "https://www.repmarcanderson.com/PropertyTaxElimination",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Property Tax Elimination\nNo senior citizen should lose the house they’ve lived in and worked for due to their inability to pay property taxes. Nor should young people be prohibited from purchasing a home and starting their independent lives due to and excessive property tax burden. This infographic provides a brief overview of the identical bills. Senate Bill 962, introduced in the Senate by Sen Dawn Keefer, and House Bill 1649, introduced by Rep. Wendy Fink. The Property Tax Elimination Act is a significant attempt to offer solutions and initiate a serious discussion on this issue.\nPlease visit here for more information on how  the Property Tax Elimination Act\nfulfills our constitutional obligation to fund education, lowers the tax burden for 85% of taxpayers, and eliminates threats to current property owners and financial obstacles for potential property owners. The website includes a\ntax calculator\nso you can see exactly how this legislation impacts you.\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Pennsylvania legislators Rep. Wendy Fink and Sen. Dawn Keefer introduced companion bills (House Bill 1649 and Senate Bill 962) called the Property Tax Elimination Act, which would eliminate property taxes and replace that education funding through another mechanism. The release promotes an informational infographic and website about the legislation, including a tax calculator.",
