  {
    "title": "Anderson Announces $550,000 for Susquehanna Area Regional Airport Authority",
    "url": "https://repmarcanderson.com/News/37329/Press-Releases/Anderson-Announces--550-000-for-Susquehanna-Area-Regional-Airport-Authority",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Anderson Announces $550,000 for Susquehanna Area Regional Airport Authority\nJanuary 21, 2026\nHARRISBURG – Rep. Marc Anderson (R-York) today announced a $550,000 Multimodal Transportation Fund grant for the Susquehanna Area Regional Airport Authority to help make needed improvements at Capital City Airport in Fairview Township. Funding was appropriated by the Commonwealth Financing Authority (CFA), an independent agency that administers Pennsylvania’s economic stimulus packages.\nThe funding will specifically be used to restore the airport’s apron, which is showing extensive wear and is in critical need of renovation to continue supporting the airport’s operations. Capital City Airport is a critical link in the regional transportation network, with 115 based aircraft and approximately 24,500 operations conducted out of the airport annually. The project will include removing and replacing deteriorated pavement, repairing the underlying base structure and upgrading related infrastructure, including stormwater drainage systems. Improvements include the installation of new asphalt binder and wearing courses, subbase reconstruction where needed, inlet adjustments, tie-down installation and permanent pavement markings.\n“I was so pleased the Commonwealth Financing Authority approved this needed funding for the airport,” said Anderson. “I had the opportunity to visit the airport earlier this month and although it is a smaller regional airport, I learned just how critical it is to our area’s transportation infrastructure. The airport supports public safety, flight training, executive travel and general aviation services across the entire region. Maintaining safe operations at the airport is essential.”\nMultimodal Transportation Fund grants can be used for the development, rehabilitation and enhancement of transportation assets to existing communities, streetscape, lighting, sidewalk enhancement, pedestrian safety, connectivity of transportation assets and transit-oriented development.\nRepresentative Marc Anderson\n92nd District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nrepmarcanderson.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Marc Anderson announced that the Commonwealth Financing Authority approved a $550,000 state grant for the Susquehanna Area Regional Airport Authority. The funds will be used to repair and replace deteriorated pavement and related infrastructure on the aircraft apron at Capital City Airport in Fairview Township. Anderson's role was to announce the grant; the funding decision was made by the independent CFA.",
      "action_type": "other",
      "topics": [
        "infrastructure",
        "economy"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Anderson Appointed to PSERS Board",
    "url": "https://repmarcanderson.com/News/37249/Press-Releases/Anderson-Appointed-to-PSERS-Board",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Anderson Appointed to PSERS Board\nJanuary 12, 2026\nHARRISBURG – State Rep. Marc Anderson (R-York) has been appointed to the Pennsylvania Public School Employees' Retirement System (PSERS) Board by the speaker of the Pennsylvania House of Representatives. He was appointed to replace former state Rep. Torren Ecker, who resigned recently after he was elected to serve as judge of the Court of Common Pleas in the 51st Judicial District.\n“As a former public school teacher, I understand how vital a secure retirement system is for educators and school employees,” said Anderson. “I’m honored to serve on the PSERS Board and will work hard to protect both the interests of our members and the taxpayers who support the system. My goal is to ensure PSERS remains strong, transparent and accountable for the benefit of all Pennsylvanians.”\nThe appointment came at the recommendation of Rep. Jesse Topper (R-Bedford/Fulton), leader of the House of Representatives Republican Caucus.\n“I have full faith that Rep. Anderson will serve with distinction on the board and will work diligently to protect taxpayers, as well as members of the system,” Topper said. “Proper legislative oversight is key in ensuring the system continues to fulfill its financial obligations to its members and I believe Rep. Anderson will handle those duties well.”\nThe board is an independent administrative body of the Commonwealth, composed of 15 members. As fiduciaries of the Pennsylvania Public School Employees’ Retirement System, board members are responsible for the investment and disbursement of fund assets. Acting as trustees, they have exclusive authority over the fund’s management and full discretion to invest its assets.\nThe board also performs other functions, such as certifying contribution rates, authorizing the actuarial valuation and independent audit of the system, and publishing an annual financial statement of the condition of the retirement fund. In addition, the board reviews the activities performed by the system's executive director and chief investment officer.\nPSERS, founded in 1917, began operations in 1919 to oversee a statewide defined benefit pension plan for public school employees. PSERS' role expanded upon the passage of Act 5 of 2017 to include oversight of two new benefit options consisting of defined benefit and defined contribution (DC) components and a stand-alone DC plan.\nAs of June 30, 2025, PSERS had a total net position of about $83.7 billion and a membership of about 262,000 active members, 255,000 annuitants and beneficiaries, and 26,000 vested inactive members.\nRepresentative Marc Anderson\n92nd District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nrepmarcanderson.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Rep. Marc Anderson (R-York) was appointed by the House Speaker to fill a vacant seat on the PSERS Board, which oversees an $83.7 billion pension fund for Pennsylvania public school employees. The appointment was recommended by House Republican Caucus Leader Jesse Topper and fills the seat left by former Rep. Torren Ecker, who recently became a judge. As a board member, Anderson will share fiduciary responsibility for managing retirement fund investments and oversight for roughly 543,000 current and former school employees.",
      "action_type": "other",
      "topics": [
        "education",
        "economy"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
